  "records": [
    {
      "key": "theol-1",
      "label": "Section 1 — Theology names speech about God, and stands to faith as science to understanding",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-2",
      "label": "Section 2 — Theology is not required of every person for salvation, yet the church cannot stand without it",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-3",
      "label": "Section 3 — The church has never lacked teachers above the faithful people; faith itself requires theological science in the church",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-4",
      "label": "Section 4 — Theology is not a science by Aristotle's strict definition, yet it is rightly called science by the evidence of the consequence",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-5",
      "label": "Section 5 — Theology is one science by species under divine revelation, and is practical rather than merely speculative",
      "paragraphs": 5,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-6",
      "label": "Section 6 — The object of theology is God as the savior of men, not deity considered apart from that respect",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-7",
      "label": "Section 7 — Theology's dignity appears from its object — above metaphysics, and wide through creatures, ethics, and history",
      "paragraphs": 5,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-8",
      "label": "Section 8 — Theology is also commended by its author — God, not Aristotle or Euclid",
      "paragraphs": 2,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-9",
      "label": "Section 9 — Theology surpasses the other sciences in certainty, both in the object and in the habit of faith",
      "paragraphs": 2,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-10",
      "label": "Section 10 — Theology's dignity shines most in its end and use — perfect beatitude, not a particular good of this life",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-11",
      "label": "Section 11 — Theology is wisely called wisdom: hardest mysteries, and independent of every other science",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-12",
      "label": "Section 12 — Theology uses the natural sciences as mistress, judges them, and rightly bears the title Wisdom",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-13",
      "label": "Section 13 — Faith is assent to God speaking, moved by divine authority — and not every assent counts as faith",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-14",
      "label": "Section 14 — Historical faith names idle assent; temporary faith is shallow joy that collapses under the cross",
      "paragraphs": 4,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-15",
      "label": "Section 15 — Miracle-working faith is a special gift; justifying faith is named; Rome confuses it with historical faith",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-16",
      "label": "Section 16 — Justifying faith must be distinguished from historical faith; Rome's reply helps; miracle faith is not an eminent grade of justifying faith",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-17",
      "label": "Section 17 — Justifying faith applies the word to practice; it includes the lesser species as the perfect includes the imperfect; assurance of pardon is not its primary act",
      "paragraphs": 3,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    },
    {
      "key": "theol-18",
      "label": "Section 18 — Faith's object is what God has revealed; Bellarmine misstates it; primary and secondary objects; explicit and implicit faith; revelation measures explicitness; implicit faith is no pretext for ignorance",
      "paragraphs": 6,
      "source": "theses_theologia_english.json"
    }
  ]
}